  <section class="section section--soft" data-nav-label="Order Flow" id="workflow">
  <div class="page-shell">
  <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal="">Example OMS-style workflow</p>
  <h2 class="section-title" data-reveal="">An order comes in. The workflow already knows where it should go.</h2>
  <p class="section-copy" data-reveal="">This is one example of what the automation add-on can do. Your rules can be different. The point is to remove the repetitive decisions and copying your operations team performs on every order.</p>
  <div class="workflow-board" data-reveal="">
  <div class="workflow-track">
  <article class="workflow-step"><span class="workflow-step__index">01</span><h3>Order enters from any company store</h3><p>Orders from multiple Shopify company stores arrive in the central platform.</p><span class="workflow-step__dot"></span></article>
  <article class="workflow-step"><span class="workflow-step__index">02</span><h3>Middleware checks your routing rules</h3><p>The workflow identifies the approved supplier, store rules, products, and required downstream path.</p><span class="workflow-step__dot"></span></article>
  <article class="workflow-step"><span class="workflow-step__index">03</span><h3>Order is split by supplier</h3><p>If one Shopify order contains products from multiple approved suppliers, the workflow can separate the work automatically.</p><span class="workflow-step__dot"></span></article>
  <article class="workflow-step"><span class="workflow-step__index">04</span><h3>PO and supplier order are created</h3><p>Purchase-order data can be generated and the supplier order can be submitted through the connected supplier API.</p><span class="workflow-step__dot"></span></article>
  <article class="workflow-step"><span class="workflow-step__index">05</span><h3>Work moves to the right decorator</h3><p>The order follows the decorator or fulfillment path configured for that supplier, product, store, or decoration requirement.</p><span class="workflow-step__dot"></span></article>
  <article class="workflow-step"><span class="workflow-step__index">06</span><h3>Your team sees everything in one dashboard</h3><p>Orders across all stores stay visible in one place, including flows that need human review.</p><span class="workflow-step__dot"></span></article>
  </div>
  </div>
  <p class="architecture-note" data-reveal="">Supplier order submission, status synchronization, and decorator automation depend on the APIs and technical access provided by each partner.</p>
  </div>
  </section>
