  <section class="section" data-nav-label="FAQs" id="faq">
  <div class="page-shell faq-layout">
  <div class="faq-heading" data-reveal=""><p class="eyebrow">Frequently asked questions</p><h2 class="section-title section-title--small">What distributors usually want to know first.</h2><p class="section-copy">Start with the platform. Add the complexity only when it solves a real operational problem.</p><a class="text-link" href="../book-demo/?service=enterprise-company-store-automation&amp;intent=automation"><span style="width:auto;height:auto;background:none">Automate My Company</span><span>→</span></a></div>
  <div class="faq-list">
  <details class="faq-item" data-reveal="" open=""><summary>What is the base company store platform?</summary><p>The base platform gives your team one place to see and manage multiple Shopify company stores, including centralized order visibility, store-level reporting, portfolio reporting, and operational status. You can use it without buying workflow automation.</p></details>
  <details class="faq-item" data-reveal=""><summary>Can the platform manage both SAGE-powered and regular Shopify company stores?</summary><p>Yes. The centralized platform can be designed around a portfolio that includes SAGE-powered Shopify company stores and simpler Shopify company stores, based on the data and controls available in each setup.</p></details>
  <details class="faq-item" data-reveal=""><summary>Which promotional products data systems do you connect with?</summary><p>Our promotional products data connections are built around SAGE and PromoStandards. We can also assess direct custom connections with individual suppliers when suitable APIs or technical access are available.</p></details>
  <details class="faq-item" data-reveal=""><summary>Can you connect directly with our approved suppliers?</summary><p>Yes. If a supplier provides suitable API access, we can build a custom connection for product data, order submission, purchase orders, status updates, or another agreed workflow.</p></details>
  <details class="faq-item" data-reveal=""><summary>How does order workflow automation work?</summary><p>A Shopify order can enter the middleware, be checked against your rules, split by approved supplier, converted into supplier POs or API orders, routed to the correct decorator or fulfillment path, and monitored from the central dashboard.</p></details>
  <details class="faq-item" data-reveal=""><summary>Can PunchOut be added later?</summary><p>Yes. PunchOut is an optional paid capability. Add it when a corporate client requires a procurement-connected company store. We validate the buyer system, cXML flow, authentication, cart return, purchase-order requirements, and testing process before confirming scope.</p></details>
  <details class="faq-item" data-reveal=""><summary>Can you build automation around our own workflow?</summary><p>Yes. If your distributor operation has a workflow that does not fit an off-the-shelf app, we can map the process and build a custom automation layer where the required systems provide suitable technical access.</p></details>
  <details class="faq-item" data-reveal=""><summary>Can you integrate QuickBooks, Sage Intacct, or NetSuite?</summary><p>Yes, these can be scoped as paid finance or ERP integration add-ons, subject to API access, account permissions, required data mappings, licensing, and technical review. We can also assess other accounting or ERP platforms when a practical integration path is available.</p></details><details class="faq-item" data-reveal=""><summary>Can you build AI features or connect OpenAI?</summary><p>Yes. Custom add-ons can include OpenAI-powered workflows, customer chatbots, AI calling agents, recommendation engines, internal assistants, and other automation ideas. The final scope depends on the business workflow, data access, privacy requirements, and available APIs.</p></details></div>
  </div>
